<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15827" root="رطى" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطًى</span></b>  [or, as some say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطَى</span>]: see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارط</span>:
(K:) it is of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْعَلٌ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْعَلُ</span>] for one
reason, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعْلًى</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعْلَى</span>] for another reason:
for they say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدِيمٌ مَأْرُوطٌ</span> as well as ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْطِىٌّ</span></b> , meaning <i>A hide tanned with the leaves of the tree
called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارطى</span>.

